{
  "description": "Glow fields: a screen grid of cols x rows cells of \"cell\" pixels that glowing things light up. Cell (0, 0) is at \"origin\" (pixels from the screen centre); spots are clipped to 0..extent from the origin; a lit cell becomes v - decay_step + ((rand & decay_jitter_mask) >> decay_jitter_shift) each frame, clamped to 0..255. The grid is drawn as Gouraud quads (prim_code is the top byte of their colour words) with a page packet (mode_tpage, dither mode_dtd) in draw-order slot \"slot\"; shade is the colour ramp by brightness; fold_peak mirrors the ramp for meshes coloured from the cells. Each field in \"fields\" is named; the name is what scripts use (sh.effects.glow_*). Every key is checked. A mod replaces the whole file with its own copy at the same path.",
